## Track B: High-Availability Multi-Master Bootstrapping

For HA environments (`preprod-ha`), execute these steps across control planes:

### 1. High Availability Architecture

The HA topology distributes apiserver requests across 3 control planes through a shared virtual IP:
- **Floating VIP**: `{{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_vip }}:{{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_port }}` managed by Keepalived VRRP.
- **Load Balancer**: Co-located HAProxy listening on `:{{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_port }}` forwarding to local `:6443`.

Verify VIP reachability before starting:

```bash
nc -zvw3 {{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_vip }} {{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_port }} || true
```

### 2. Initialize Primary Control Plane (`kube-cp-1`)

On `kube-cp-1`, initialize the cluster specifying `--control-plane-endpoint` and `--upload-certs`:

```bash
cd ~/cka/00-cluster-installation
sudo ./01-ha-kubeadm-init.sh
```

Or execute manually:

```bash
sudo kubeadm init \
  --control-plane-endpoint="{{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_vip }}:{{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_port }}" \
  --upload-certs \
  --pod-network-cidr="{{ cka_lab_cluster_install_pod_cidr }}" \
  --service-cidr="{{ cka_lab_cluster_install_service_cidr }}"
```

### 3. Join Secondary Control Planes (`kube-cp-2`, `kube-cp-3`)

Retrieve the control plane join command generated during `kubeadm init` (contains `--control-plane --certificate-key`).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> You **must** supply `--apiserver-advertise-address <joining_node_ip>` matching each node's cluster interface
> (`192.168.56.11` on `kube-cp-2` and `192.168.56.12` on `kube-cp-3`). Omitting this flag causes `kubeadm` to bind
> to the default NAT interface, stalling the join on etcd cluster health.

Execute on **`kube-cp-2`** (`192.168.56.11`):

```bash
sudo kubeadm join {{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_vip }}:{{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_port }} \
  --token <token> \
  --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:<hash> \
  --control-plane \
  --certificate-key <key> \
  --apiserver-advertise-address 192.168.56.11
```

Execute on **`kube-cp-3`** (`192.168.56.12`):

```bash
sudo kubeadm join {{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_vip }}:{{ cka_lab_ha_cluster_port }} \
  --token <token> \
  --discovery-token-ca-cert-hash sha256:<hash> \
  --control-plane \
  --certificate-key <key> \
  --apiserver-advertise-address 192.168.56.12
```

### 4. Verify Stacked etcd Quorum

Verify that all 3 control plane members participate in the etcd quorum:

```bash
sudo ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl \
  --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt \
  --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt \
  --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key \
  --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 \
  endpoint health
```

